 "background": "Word arrives from Thessaloniki: the Turks have set up a gallows to hang Goce Delčev. Goce disguises himself as a little black coal-man and strolls through the Thessaloniki bazaar. Soldiers ask him whether he has seen Goce Delčev, and he answers that even if he saw him, he would not recognise him. Qwen adds that Delčev was killed in May 1903 near the village of Banitsa (I have not checked this).",
